{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following MS C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original MS C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nusing ll = long long;\nusing ld = long double;\n\nll my_gcd(ll a, ll b) {\n    for (ll t; b; t = b, b = a % b, a = t);\n    return a;\n}\n\nll my_lcm(ll a, ll b) {\n    return a / my_gcd(a, b) * b;\n}\n\nld my_diff(ll n1, ll d1, ll n2, ll d2) {\n    ll cd = my_lcm(d1, d2);\n    ll num1 = cd / d1 * n1;\n    ll num2 = cd / d2 * n2;\n    return abs(num1 - num2) / ld(cd);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n#ifndef ONLINE_JUDGE\n    freopen(\"input.txt\", \"r\", stdin);\n    freopen(\"output.txt\", \"w\", stdout);\n#endif\n\n    ll x, y, n;\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    ll best_n = 0, best_d = 1;\n    ld target = ld(x) / y;\n    \n    for (ll d = 1; d <= n; ++d) {\n        ll left = 1, right = 1000000;\n        while (right - left > 1) {\n            ll mid = (left + right) / 2;\n            ld val = ld(mid) / d;\n            if (val < target) left = mid;\n            else right = mid;\n        }\n        \n        ll candidate = (my_diff(left, d, x, y) > my_diff(right, d, x, y)) ? right : left;\n        if (my_diff(candidate, d, x, y) < my_diff(best_n, best_d, x, y)) {\n            best_n = candidate;\n            best_d = d;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << best_n << \"/\" << best_d;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport math\n\ndef my_gcd(a, b):\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    return a\n\ndef my_lcm(a, b):\n    return a // my_gcd(a, b) * b\n\ndef my_diff(n1, d1, n2, d2):\n    cd = my_lcm(d1, d2)\n    num1 = cd // d1 * n1\n    num2 = cd // d2 * n2\n    return abs(num1 - num2) / cd\n\ndef main():\n    x, y, n = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    best_n = 0\n    best_d = 1\n    target = x / y\n    \n    for d in range(1, n + 1):\n        left = 1\n        right = 1000000\n        while right - left > 1:\n            mid = (left + right) // 2\n            val = mid / d\n            if val < target:\n                left = mid\n            else:\n                right = mid\n        \n        candidate = right if my_diff(left, d, x, y) > my_diff(right, d, x, y) else left\n        if my_diff(candidate, d, x, y) < my_diff(best_n, best_d, x, y):\n            best_n = candidate\n            best_d = d\n    \n    print(f\"{best_n}/{best_d}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.868777513271198e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.008742273785173893, -0.4743405282497406, -0.17977233231067657, -7.152531907195225e-06, -0.0011076750233769417, -4.768360213347478e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.00023052419419400394, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -7.271740287251305e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00021824838768225163, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.8358061424805783e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.009768186137080193, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.1920